# Build output
/target

# Where `make bin` and `make dist` put a release build and its tarball.
# See scripts/build.sh.
/bin/
/dist/

# Editor and OS cruft
/.vscode/
/.idea/
*.rs.bk
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Snapshots written by the `P` key. With `[export] dir` unset — the default —
# these land in the working directory, which is the checkout while developing.
# One rule per `export::ExportFormat`; see `export::export_path`.
/crabmon-*.json
/crabmon-*.csv
/crabmon-*.txt

# Session recordings from `--record`, the rotating segments from
# `--record-rotate`, and the flight recorder's dumps — with `[record]
# flight_dir` unset, those land in the working directory too, named by
# `record::dump_name` and `record::segment_name`.
#
# Unanchored, and it has to stay that way: a fleet export records a timeline
# per host, which is `run-web-1.jsonl` beside the path `--record` names and a
# directory per host — `web-1/crabmon-<unix>.jsonl` — under the one
# `--record-rotate` names. An anchored rule would catch neither. The host part
# is whatever `record::unique_labels` made of the target, so it may be
# `deploy-db-2-2` where two targets collided or `host-1` where one had no
# usable characters at all; `tests/docs.rs` checks those shapes too.
*.jsonl

# The human-readable incident summary written beside every flight dump, by
# `incident::path_for`. Unanchored, because it follows the dump wherever
# `flight_dir` puts it — but narrow enough not to swallow README.md or
# anything under docs/.
crabmon-*.md

# A Unix socket from `--serve unix:...` with a relative path.
*.sock

# The temporary file `config::save_to` renames over the real config. It only
# survives a crash mid-save, and only lands here when `--config` points into
# the checkout.
*.toml.*.tmp

# Action log, when `[audit] path` points somewhere relative, or when no
# platform state directory can be resolved and it falls back to `./crabmon/`.
/actions.log
/crabmon/

# `cargo vendor`, which docs/DESIGN.md names as the way to close the last
# network dependency in the e2e image build. 446 MB of dependencies is not
# something to drop into a review by accident. `.cargo/` is deliberately not
# ignored: a `config.toml` there is usually meant to be committed.
/vendor/

# Profiling output
perf.data*
flamegraph.svg
